    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0360" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5752/1</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                        1925</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 22.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 595</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that, in
                    compliance with the Department’s Instruction No. 221, of April 21, 1925,<anchor
                        n="52" xml:id="d166-f1"/> I addressed to the Madrid Foreign Office a Note,
                    No. 316, dated May 8, 1925, from the enclosed copy of which<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d166-f2"/> it will be seen that I informed the Acting Foreign
                    Minister of the appointment of a Customs Attaché and three Assistants to this
                    Embassy, and requested recognition of them in their respective capacities by the
                    Spanish Government.</p>
                <p>A copy and translation of the Note of reply of the Foreign Office are transmitted
                        herewith.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d166-f3"/> In it I am advised that the
                    Spanish Government, while not according to the officials in reference the status
                    of attachés to this Embassy, is willing to grant to them, upon request, such
                    customs facilities as are usually extended to members <pb facs="0361" n="235"
                        xml:id="pg235"/> of diplomatic missions, if in the discharge of their duties
                    they are required to visit Spain.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander P.
                    Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
